Subject: [PATCH] cli: the SSID change answers with the controller's status

The wireless profiles route (set_ssid) answered success whatever the controller said: an SSID
change it refused, or one it took into its model but did not carry out, looked applied, and a
lab was left on a test SSID after its restore "succeeded". applyNetworkNameConfig now returns
the controller's status and the route answers with it (set_ssid_status.go): 200 for Success or
no change, 409 when a change or a radio's configuration is in progress, 422 when refused, 503
when not ready.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
index b18022b..c30657d 100644
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -2039,16 +2039,12 @@ func getWirelessProfilesHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
                 }
             }
 
-            if applyNetworkNameConfig(ssidTree) != true {
-                http.Error(w, fmt.Sprintf("Failed to update networkssid list"), http.StatusInternalServerError)
-            }
-
-            // Return success response
+            // the controller's answer, not success whatever it said (set_ssid_status.go)
+            status, err := applyNetworkNameConfig(ssidTree)
+            code, reply := setSSIDReply(status, err)
             w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
-            json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(map[string]interface{}{
-                "success": true,
-                "message": "Profile updated successfully",
-            })
